ion  suggests that it won't be sufficient on  its own to  flatten the peak and reduce the pressure  on the health system  and on people being off work  do you support would you support chris  woody's advice  reduce the number of households that mix  try and avoid  essentially social contact social mixing  if you can over the next period  yes i mean what chris whittake said and  you know he is the nation's public  health doctor um and he's giving uh  excellent public health advice is that  you know reduce your contacts to those  that really matter to you so you know  the less the better but i mean this is  the second christmas that has the  potential to be significantly ruined for  a number of people  and so you know there are also the  health issues of not being able to see  your loved ones but so you know the  answer is to uh be prudent um and  you know only have the social contacts  which are really important to you  you've you've had the task of trying to  evaluate  significant  level amounts of scientific  data for government and advice ministers  and so on that is proving crucial right  now  there is a major issue about the  modeling uh that is that is emerging  from various sources um  i put to the health sector this morning  what uh the chair of the modern  committee of sage said which is that we  are generally asked to model uh we are  generally modeling what we are asked to  model  in a sense what he's saying is that  there is uh  the evidence that is being produced  is that which the politicians are asking  in order to support further restrictions  uh does that make sense to you that  actually what's happening here  it doesn't make any sense at all  actually um i mean the model is i mean  the first thing to do is say that the  modelers produce projections they don't  produce predictions  and all of the models have wide  uncertainties attached to them as well  and this has been no different  throughout this pandemic at all i mean  what the modelers are bein