 are rising fast we have  a new variant we have pressure on the  health service with increased hospital  admissions  uh the risks are that because of the lag  and that's always the challenge that  people you know forget each time that  from the moment you get an infection  become symptomatic to when you may have  to go into hospital is a week to ten  days or so and then it's another you  know two or three weeks before uh the  worst effects of the infection  particularly death may occur  and so you know if you're going to act  you actually have to act in advance and  that's one of the difficult things but  you know the job of the scientists is to  actually provide the evidence for the  policy makers the policy makers our  politicians and therefore ultimately the  decisions are political decisions but  there's no pressure on sage or sage  advisors or the modelers to do anything  other than provide the best possible  evidence you know given that there are  uncertainties at any moment  so mark thank you so much for your time  this morning much appreciated

